INT. PIEROGI FACTORY - NIGHT SHIFT

Steam. Conveyor belts of dough. Hairnets and hum.

RAFAL KOWALCZYK (40s, detective, rumpled suit under a hairnet) squints at a freezer door. TAMSIN OKORO (30s, factory floor manager, clipboard, no patience) walks beside him.

TAMSIN
Four minutes.

RAFAL
You said that at the gate.

TAMSIN
Four minutes at the gate. Four minutes now.

They pass a bin of spinach filling. Rafal sniffs it. Winces.

RAFAL
Who found the body?

TAMSIN
Night packer. Quit on the spot.

RAFAL
Name?

TAMSIN
Gus. Everybody calls him the Ferret.

Rafal nods. Writes.

A belt jams. Alarm bleats. Tamsin pivots and kills it with one slap.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
(to the floor)
Back to your stations. Nothing to see.

Workers drift. Rafal watches them go.

RAFAL
Nothing.

TAMSIN
I run a clean line.

RAFAL
Somebody stuffed a man into your freezer.

TAMSIN
Not on my line.

At the end of the corridor, a hairnet bobs. GUS "THE FERRET" LINDGREN (50s, wiry, sleeves pulled over fists) hurries toward the exit.

RAFAL
Hey.

Gus quickens.

RAFAL (CONT'D)
Mr. Lindgren.

Gus sprints. Rafal vaults a bin of dough. Tamsin swears and follows.

INT. LOADING DOCK - CONTINUOUS

Gus slams through the door and runs headlong into BIANCA DELACROIX-OYELARAN (30s, health inspector, white coat, clipboard of her own). Both go down.

BIANCA
Watch it!

GUS
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

Rafal arrives, breathing hard. Tamsin right behind.

RAFAL
Stay on the floor, both of you.

TAMSIN
(to Bianca)
You are early.

BIANCA
(to Tamsin)
You are in violation.

RAFAL
(to Gus)
Where were you going?

GUS
Home. I didn't see nothing.

RAFAL
You saw the body.

GUS
I saw a coat.

BIANCA
What body?

TAMSIN
There is no body.

RAFAL
There is a body.

TAMSIN
^There is no body, and you have no warrant.

They talk over each other. Gus scrambles up. Bianca writes. Rafal grabs Gus by the sleeve.

RAFAL
Whose coat?

GUS
(wet-eyed)
Hers.

He points. At Tamsin.

The loading dock goes quiet. A forklift beeps somewhere. Tamsin looks at her own coat. Zipped to the chin. Dry-cleaned. Perfect.

TAMSIN
That is a lie.

BIANCA
(pen hovering)
Is it?

Tamsin steps backward. Rafal steps with her.

RAFAL
Open the coat.

TAMSIN
I will not.

RAFAL
Open it.

She doesn't. Gus whimpers. Bianca flips a page. Rafal reaches for the zipper.

Tamsin's hand snaps out and clamps his wrist. Her knuckles whiten. For a heartbeat they stand locked like dancers.

Then she lets go. Slides the zipper down. Underneath, the lining is torn, dark, and wet.

TAMSIN
He wasn't supposed to be on shift.
